tools.description:
Apply one surgical draft chart op (add_seat | connect | insert_stage | set_agent | reorder_stages). Requires draft session + CAS. Refusals return a sentence. Never Applies, binds a live terminal, or starts a team.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__onedevtool__orchestration_chart_op(args: {
  basePolicyHash: string;
  baseRevision: number;
  // Chart op payload with an "op" discriminator
  op: { [key: string]: unknown; };
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Propose a whole hierarchy or pipeline chart from mermaid flowchart source into the Builder draft. Requires a human-enabled draft session and basePolicyHash/baseRevision. Never Applies, Activates, or Starts a team.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__onedevtool__orchestration_propose_chart(args: {
  // CAS: current draft policy hash from orchestration_explain
  basePolicyHash: string;
  // CAS: current draft revision
  baseRevision: number;
  // Mermaid flowchart source
  source: string;
  // Chart topology
  topology: "hierarchy" | "pipeline";
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Recommend Builder canvas topology for a setup description: hierarchy | pipeline | router | ephemeral-team | none. Read-only; never writes a chart. ephemeral-team / none mean prose dispatch, not a durable chart.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__onedevtool__orchestration_recommend(args: {
  // What the user wants to set up
  text: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Report a task finished, with a summary against its acceptance criteria. Either closes it or opens a done gate for review.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__onedevtool__tasks_complete(args: {
  id: string;
  // What you did, against the acceptance criteria
  summary: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Create a task in this terminal's project. Created unassigned — a human decides who works on it.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__onedevtool__tasks_create(args: {
  // What must be true for this to be done
  acceptanceCriteria?: Array<string>;
  // Markdown detail
  body?: string;
  labels?: Array<string>;
  // Parent task id, for a subtask
  parent?: string;
  priority?: "p0" | "p1" | "p2" | "p3";
  // One line, imperative
  title: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Get one task in full: body, acceptance criteria, definition of done, plan, dependencies and recent activity.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__onedevtool__tasks_get(args: {
  // Task id, e.g. t-7k2m9qx4wp3fn
  id: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

List tasks as compact rows without bodies. Use to see the board; use tasks_get for one task in full.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__onedevtool__tasks_list(args: {
  // true = only blocked, false = only unblocked
  blocked?: boolean;
  // Filter by a single label
  label?: string;
  // Maximum rows (capped at 100)
  limit?: number;
  // Only tasks assigned to this terminal
  mine?: boolean;
  // Filter by priority
  priority?: Array<"p0" | "p1" | "p2" | "p3">;
  // Defaults to this terminal's project
  scope?: "project" | "all";
  // Filter by status
  status?: Array<"backlog" | "ready" | "in_progress" | "blocked" | "in_review" | "done" | "cancelled">;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Get the next task assigned to this terminal. Empty means stop and report back — it never means look for other work. Use at the start of a fresh session, or after finishing a task.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__onedevtool__tasks_next(args: {
  // Which projects to consider. Defaults to this terminal's project.
  scope?: "project" | "all";
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Ask the human to approve a plan or answer a question. Returns a gateId immediately; poll tasks_wait for the verdict.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__onedevtool__tasks_request_approval(args: {
  // Task id
  id: string;
  // 'plan' before implementing, 'question' any time
  kind: "plan" | "question" | "done";
  // Optional choices, for a question
  options?: Array<string>;
  // The plan, the question, or what you want reviewed
  payload: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```

Update a task assigned to you: status, priority, labels, body, plan, or tick acceptance criteria. Cannot set who a task is assigned to.

exec tool declaration:
```ts
declare const tools: { mcp__onedevtool__tasks_update(args: {
  // The hash from tasks_get — proves you are editing what you read
  baseHash?: string;
  body?: string;
  // 1-based indexes of criteria now satisfied
  criteriaDone?: Array<number>;
  id: string;
  labels?: Array<string>;
  // Your implementation plan
  plan?: string;
  priority?: "p0" | "p1" | "p2" | "p3";
  status?: "backlog" | "ready" | "in_progress" | "blocked" | "in_review" | "done" | "cancelled";
  title?: string;
}): Promise<CallToolResult>; };
```
